<title>ITALY: Fiat '96 extra capital gains 1.55 trln lire.</title>
<headline>Fiat '96 extra capital gains 1.55 trln lire.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial group Fiat had net extraordinary capital gains of about 1.554 trillion lire in 1996, according to preliminary data contained in documents prepared for presentation to U.S. institutional investors.</p>
<p>The capital gain from the flotation of 31 percent of Fiat's truck and construction vehicle unit New Holland was 1.109 trillion while sale of its Prime unit brought 253 billion.</p>
<p>Real estate operations yielded 18 billion while other gains totalled 174 billion.</p>
<p>Fiat released preliminary 1996 data at the end of January.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
